WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:37.230
Rosamia's Gaplant and
Buran Blutarch's Asshimar...

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.170
...struck the Audhumla in waves.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.270
During this attack, Amuro and Katz
flew a freighter into the middle of the battle.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:50.610
Thus Amuro Ray joined
Hayato and the others.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.580
Katz's Sortie

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.900
As long as it moves.
Just work on the critical repairs.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.830
- I plan to go right back out.
- Yes, sir.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.500
<i>Who would've expected</i>
<i>to be rammed by a freighter?</i>

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.540
Major!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.040
Major Buran Blutarch!

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.740
It's all thanks to you, Major...

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.010
...that I'm able to have repairs
done to my Gaplant.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.350
<i>Is it a habit of the Cyber-Newtype</i>
<i>to repeat something over and over?</i>

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.390
Major.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.360
Please let me join your team, sir.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:37.520
Major!

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.560
I want to defeat those people
no matter what it takes.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.930
Those people?

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.430
I don't like the way you said that.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.840
I'm sorry.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.370
But I just can't endure it.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.240
That those people make the sky fall!

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.780
Make the sky fall?

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:56.780
Isn't that right?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.320
The A.E.U.G. is a group of people who
want to eradicate the people of Earth...

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.150
...by dropping a colony on them.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.190
The sight of a colony falling...!

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.080
It's as if the sky were falling!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.060
Such a sight...!

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.960
The A.E.U.G. is a group of people who
hate the thought of polluting Earth.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.530
They wouldn't go to that extent.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.430
Even now, I dream of it every night.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.700
A dream of the sky falling!

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.740
I understand, Ensign.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.570
Do as you wish.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.410
Thank you very much!

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.390
I see, so they've gone to Japan.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.300
Yeah.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.830
Was it your idea for Fraw
to come see me, Hayato?

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.200
Did it annoy you?

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.000
No.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.040
I'm glad I sent them to you, Amuro.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.740
You brought Katz here, as I expected.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.870
What do you mean by that?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:06.110
He was dying to get away from life on Earth.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.810
But Fraw hated the idea.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.650
I don't blame her.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.660
There's no mother in the world
who'd want to send her child to war.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:13.660
Right.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.960
And it's no different for a foster mother.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:19.660
But a child will do as he wishes,
regardless of how the parents feel.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.100
When I see Katz, I feel that I've aged.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.170
I hoped I wouldn't be hearing
such pessimistic comments from you.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.840
I'm hoping you'll have a hand
in training Katz.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.300
Actually, it's the other way around, right?

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.140
You really want to retrain me, right?

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.010
Yes?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.880
<i>If you have a moment, I'd like you to help.</i>

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:39.680
Roger.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.950
- Was that Char?
- That was Lieutenant Quattro.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.320
To me, he's no one other than
Char Aznable.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.120
Don't be such a stickler about it.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.930
So this is the panoramic monitor.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.960
This is awesome!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:04:59.660
Hands off!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.100
I'm sorry.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:04.940
No, <i>I'm</i> sorry.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.440
I was making adjustments to it.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.040
You wouldn't want an electric jolt,
would you?

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.240
No.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.310
I was moved by the heroics
of this Gundam Mk. II.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.680
I'm impressed that you were piloting it!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:15.720
Kamille!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.050
- Take care of Katz!
- But...!

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.490
He knows how to operate a mobile suit.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.160
Oh, very well then.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.320
So I hear you know about mobile suits.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.830
As you know, my father's
the director of the war museum.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.230
So I've been on pretty much
all the older models.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.100
- At Kennedy?
- Yes!

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.240
Your father seems awfully young.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.770
Well, he's my foster father.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.710
Even so, it's better
than not having a father at all.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.680
Do you know Amuro Ray well?

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.880
I was always with him on the White Base
during the One Year War.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:49.980
Really?

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.250
Amuro was an idol to us.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.920
But Amuro's like a different person lately.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:58.590
But that was quite the scene when he
rammed the enemy with the freighter.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.530
However... I can't be sure yet.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.290
He doesn't have the same spirit.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.530
These new Dodais will come in handy
should we suddenly require them...!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.800
- But will they come?
- They will.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:15.340
The new model mobile suit wants
to prove its performance superiority.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.810
<i>Char, why did you return to Earth?</i>

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.820
Will we get information from Kai at Hickory?

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.420
Can't be sure.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.890
Finding the Titans' base
won't be an easy task.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.460
They say people have the tendency
to underrate the abilities...

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.460
...of their own close relatives.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.960
I guess it's true.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.900
You know, Kai was a crewmember
of the White Base.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.930
I believe in him.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:44.440
I'm sure he won't let us down.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.210
I'm impressed.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:56.650
To charge into a mobile suit with something
like a freighter that lacks mobility.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.690
Why did you return to the Earth Sphere?

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.760
I came to laugh at you.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.560
That's what you wanted to hear, isn't it?

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.430
I didn't choose to end up like this.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.020
I'm sure you understand that.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.470
And yet, you don't really want sympathy,
do you?

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.940
Then I'd like to see you
become the Amuro Ray...

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.640
...who will live up to Katz's expectations.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.630
That is the best advice I could give you.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.200
Why did you return to the Earth Sphere?!

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.480
Lalah's spirit is still drifting in
the Earth Sphere.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.520
I felt she didn't exist past Mars.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.720
Lalah.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:36.080
Shutting yourself within your shell in turn
means you'll end up...

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.360
...giving the Earth Federation Government,
no, the Titans, a helping hand.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.660
I can't do anything if I can't get into space!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.640
Remember this, "A bird in a cage
is nothing but a tool for one's enjoyment."

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:52.970
Mr. Amuro!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.000
Your late night snack.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.150
Right, thanks.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.980
I've been hoping for the chance to meet you.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:06.480
I hear your name from various people.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.580
I've felt people have been comparing
me to you. It's been a pain.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.090
I want you to tell me. How can I live up to
the expectations of those around me?

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:19.460
I was about your age
when I first fought in a Gundam.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.700
Back then, I was desperate.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.140
What has Katz been saying about me?

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.340
I believe he said something to you.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.750
Then why don't you ask Katz directly?!

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:34.580
Kamille?

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.680
Excuse me!

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.020
What in the world am I doing?

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.600
That's right!

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.500
And then maintain your shooting stance,
using your hand to support you!

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.840
What if the A.E.U.G.'s Garuda
makes it across the Pacific Ocean?!

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:01.850
They won't get away
no matter where they go.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:04.180
The Forces in New Guinea
won't be sitting back either.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.370
New Guinea?

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.210
Is that a new base location?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.050
Well, yeah.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.190
Okay!

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.050
Make sure you both pay attention
to your balance!

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.310
An airplane?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.750
It's a biplane!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.090
What a beautiful sight!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.130
An airplane!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.660
Two o'clock position, below!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.100
The airplane belongs to Karaba!
I'm certain!

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.600
- Karaba?!
- Yes, sir!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.540
Father!

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.580
Okay, lower the ship, and reduce speed.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.740
- We'll have it enter from the rear hatch.
- Roger!

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:25.930
The air current...!

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.100
Is it okay?

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.140
Was that the deck?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.250
I'm sorry to wake you so early.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:00.790
I'm Beltorchika Irma of Karaba.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.230
Hickory is waiting for you.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.490
Thank you. I'm Hayato Kobayashi
of the museum.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.670
Are you Katz?

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:09.040
Huh? Ah, yes.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:10.970
Nice kid! Pleased to meet you!

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.350
What an airplane!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.180
Oh, Kamille!

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.180
This is Beltorchika Irma of Karaba.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.040
You like my airplane?

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.920
- It's a beautiful replica.
- Thank you.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:28.490
Where's Amuro?

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.030
- Go and wake him up.
- Right!

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.090
It's not only the Beechcraft...

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:35.130
...but the lady called Beltorchika
seems to be a wonderful person.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:37.430
What happened to you yesterday?

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.030
Aren't you interested in the Gundam?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.040
Are you bothered that they made
the Mk. II?

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.870
Shut up, already! Leave me alone!

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:49.940
As you wish!

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:55.850
<i>These are insinuating actions</i>
<i>on Char and Hayato's part...</i>

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:59.050
<i>...to let a younger guy pilot the Gundam</i>
<i>while ignoring me.</i>

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:17.200
The shuttle at Hickory is capable
of sending three mobile suits to space.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.610
Oh, Amuro. This person here...!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.410
I heard from Katz.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.370
Pleased to meet you.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.580
- I'm Amuro Ray.
- Amuro?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.440
So you're Amuro.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.890
That's Helen-Helen, isn't it?

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.380
My favorite soap brand.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:37.360
Oh.

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:40.330
So, you're Amuro Ray. Hmm...!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.860
Why do we have Helen-Helen
on the Audhumla?

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.800
Beats me!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.600
Now, help yourself, Amuro Ray.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:50.970
- You brought these?
- Yes.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.540
You're a Newtype, but you
look like a normal person.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.470
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:03.890
You know, I'd always imagined
Amuro Ray to be more war-like.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:05.950
I'm relieved.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.720
I was worried to think, what if
the A.E.U.G. and Karaba were...

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:14.290
...unconcerned about killing people, hiding
behind the excuse that there's just cause...

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.160
...like the Titans... no, the Earth Federation
Government has been doing?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.560
- I was scared.
- And?

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:26.240
Who's that person wearing the sunglasses?

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.240
That's Lieutenant Quattro of the A.E.U.G..

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.680
He's in charge of this operation.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.010
<i>What's she afraid of?</i>

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.990
Why won't you join them over there?

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.620
I don't want to be with Mr. Amuro.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.600
San Francisco?

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:46.760
In five minutes.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:49.620
Although there isn't any city there.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.700
He seems like a scary person, with a glare.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.530
He looks like the type of person
who can't live without war.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.470
You're a member of Karaba yourself.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.870
You can't be totally against fighting either.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:02.510
However...

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.210
...with that person, I don't sense
any peaceful intelligence.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.510
Lt. Quattro's not the type of person
you think he is.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:10.680
Deep inside, he's a very kind person!

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:22.190
Did I say something that I shouldn't have?

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.290
No.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.830
Don't worry about it, Beltorchika.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:30.540
That's a lie!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.930
- An enemy!
- A pursuer?!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.610
- Ensign Rosamia's going?!
- Yes, sir!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.910
I must repay you
for taking us in!

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.490
- How many enemies?!
- <i>Just one, sir! Very persistent!</i>

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.050
- I'm going to use this one!
- Go ahead!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.000
I should be able to fight, too!

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.840
Kamille?!

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.210
Who's in it?!

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.300
The Gundam Mk. II is moving!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.280
Who's in it?!

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:46.980
<i>Katz, taking off!</i>

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:49.850
Katz?! No way!

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.150
Not an actual battle!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.350
Open the hatch!

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:56.390
How'd you like that?!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:02.860
Kamille!

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:04.370
Can you sortie in the Rick Dias?

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.400
Roger!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.470
Did Katz just go?!

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.800
- Katz went?!
- Katz?!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.810
Katz is that young boy, right?

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:14.670
Forget it!

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.270
You've got to be kidding!

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:19.040
You haven't touched a mobile suit
for seven years, right?!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.610
At least Katz has had training on it!

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.550
You can stay and defend!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.920
But I used to be a Gundam pilot!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:26.560
Amuro Ray.

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:29.480
<i>So this person was also a pilot...!</i>

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.860
<i>Just another person who fights.</i>

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.960
Kamille left in the Rick Dias!

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.160
All units, back him up!

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:44.940
<i>What?</i>

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:49.040
<i>The same individual who said he's</i>
<i>going out to fight is now trembling in fear.</i>

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.720
<i>Is this the same person</i>
<i>people referred to as a Newtype?</i>

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.850
<i>Yeah, just like I'm afraid</i>
<i>of the sky falling...</i>

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:04.730
<i>...this man's afraid of fighting.</i>

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:06.790
Shall we fly or descend?

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:07.760
We'll descend.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.390
I can't grasp the number
of enemy units attacking!

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.570
But I don't want to die.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.120
It looks like two units took off.
Do they have any chance against me?

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.960
Where's the enemy?
Will it attack from the right?

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.630
Or the left?

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.500
Do Hizacks attack from above?!

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:55.570
Darn! Which one's
the enemy search monitor?!

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:57.170
This is different from a Zaku!

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:58.550
Is that it?!

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:08.360
You're not getting away this time.
I don't repeat my mistakes.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.590
Behind me?!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:24.270
Is that not the same pilot from yesterday?

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.940
Or perhaps this is part of some strategy!

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.920
<i>No matter what your strategy may be...!</i>

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.450
No, it's definitely a different pilot.

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:56.540
Wh-What was that?!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.440
The golden mobile suit?!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.480
Then I'll use that Gundam as a shield!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:11.320
It's escaping?!

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:12.620
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:15.060
- Look after Katz and the Mk. II!
- Roger!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.720
Darn it! Darn it! Darn it!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:24.860
Katz!

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:26.530
Open your eyes!
Watch your opponent carefully!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:33.300
It can control a Dodai?!

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.310
What is this power?!

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.580
Katz, reposition yourself!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:50.790
<i>Katz!</i>

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.490
Kamille... in a Rick Dias?!

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:02.830
- Any pursuers?
- No sign of mobile suits coming out.

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:09.680
- Katz!
- I can still fight!

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.340
Come to your senses!

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:14.820
Don't you realize that what you've done
is causing trouble to others?!

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:19.220
<i>It's too late after the Gundam Mk. II</i>
<i>gets destroyed!</i>

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.320
I understand!

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.160
He got it?

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.230
I won't let this...!

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:36.570
How dare you attack without regard
to what's around you!

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:58.260
Was that... a woman?

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.730
How's Katz?

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.330
He's all right.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.900
What was that pilot?

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:18.570
It seems some energy has been
released from a misguided mind.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:20.140
- Don't worry about it!
- Right.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.620
Rosamia Badam.

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:29.920
Her over-aggressiveness results in defeat.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.020
Can Cyber-Newtypes really be of any use?

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.630
You fool!

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.100
Unbelievable.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:39.030
I'm sorry, Father.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:40.870
B-But... I...!

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:43.970
- I saw an enemy that wasn't visible! Really!
- Shut up!

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.410
What use is that anyway?!

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:48.840
Don't take one coincidence
and start believing...

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:51.610
...that it's some sort of ability
you've developed!

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:54.980
I think Director Hayato's right, Katz.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:57.820
On the other hand, what Katz says is true.

00:21:57.890 --> 00:22:00.720
Even so, I cannot easily forgive him
for his stupid actions.

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:05.480
At times, the selfish actions of one person
can end up wiping out a force!

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:08.060
That cannot be forgiven!

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:11.200
<i>What's wrong, Amuro?</i>

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:14.140
<i>The youngsters are out there fighting.</i>

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.500
<i>Don't you feel that sensation</i>
<i>in your blood like you did back then?</i>

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:51.110
The Audhumla remains over the west coast
to make contact with Hickory.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.770
Beltorchika presses Amuro
for a commitment...

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:57.840
...in order to fulfill the responsibilities
of returning Char and Kamille to space.

00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:02.510
Amuro then takes the Rick Dias
and battles the Asshimar.

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:07.590
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Through the Haze of Darkness".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Through the Haze of Darkness

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:12.490
You will see the tears of time.
